fluxecho.bee_imprinter.tip=§3Takes the genes of a real bee, sapling (or pollen) or butterfly, unharmed§r\nSpecial slot: the sample (or an imprint, or a gene sample); it stays there\nPaper, no circuit: an imprint of all the sample's genes\nPaper + programmed circuit: a gene sample of just the circuit's genes\nImprint of the same kind + circuit: those genes written straight onto it (species kept)\nBees: 1 speed  2 lifespan  3 fertility  4 temperature  5 nocturnal  6 humidity\n  7 rain  8 cave  9 flower  10 pollination  11 territory  12 effect\n  13 every environment gene (4-8)  14 every gene but the species\nTrees: 1-12 one gene, 14 all; butterflies: 1-13 one gene, 14 all\n%s s per run, %s EU/t
fluxecho.larva_incubator.tip=§3Grows the bee, tree or butterfly of an imprint§r\nAnalysed, pure-bred; climate does not matter\nSpecial slot: an imprint (or a real sample); it stays there\nBees (honey drops): no circuit or circuit 1 %3$s drops -> 1 pristine princess + %4$s drones; circuit 2 %5$s drops -> %6$s drones\nTrees (Forestry fertilizer): %7$s -> %8$s saplings\nButterflies (honey drops): %9$s -> %10$s butterflies\nA princess left in the output holds the next batch\n%1$s s per batch, %2$s EU/t
